speechtext:
Mr. Speaker, I rise under the provisions of Standing Order 43 to ask the unanimous consent of the House to move a motion of urgent and pressing necessity.
In so far as there has been an announcement by the Quebec Minister of Education in the Quebec National Assembly to the effect that new criteria have been agreed to relative to Opportunity for Youth projects in that province, and as the Secretary of State (Mr. Pelletier) has not informed the House of Commons of this agreement, I move, seconded by the hon. member for Lambton-Kent (Mr. McCutcheon):
That this House do direct the Secretary of State to appear before a special committee on youth established by this House for the purpose of discussing:
a)	any agreements reached with the province of Quebec concerning the Opportunities for Youth Program;
b)	the as yet unpublished evaluation of last year's Opportunities for Youth program;
c)	the task force report on youth;
d)	the planning that should be under way now for summer, 1972. Mr. Speaker: Is there unanimous consent?
